Which country gained the most?
Next I calculated the change in life expectancy for each country between 1952 and 2007.

life_change &lt;- gapminder |&gt;
  filter(year %in% c(1952, 2007)) |&gt;
  select(country, continent, year, lifeExp) |&gt;
  pivot_wider(names_from = year, values_from = lifeExp, names_prefix = "y") |&gt;
  mutate(change = y2007 - y1952) |&gt;
  arrange(desc(change))

n_declined &lt;- sum(life_change$change &lt; 0)
top &lt;- slice_head(life_change, n = 1)
bottom &lt;- slice_tail(life_change, n = 1)


bind_rows(slice_head(life_change, n = 5), slice_tail(life_change, n = 5))




Top/Bottom 5 changes in life expectancy


Oman gained the most, 38.1 years. At the other end, 2 countries had a lower life expectancy in 2007 than in 1952. The largest drop was in Zimbabwe (-5 years).
